WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.868 --> 00:00:01.934
-You look fantastic.

00:00:01.934 --> 00:00:02.934
Thank you for coming
on to the show.

00:00:02.934 --> 00:00:04.267
-Thank you.
-I appreciate this.

00:00:04.267 --> 00:00:06.968
I think the last time I saw you,
you were with your dad.

00:00:06.968 --> 00:00:08.267
Your dad was on our show.

00:00:08.267 --> 00:00:11.601
-Yes, and that was a
very embarrassing day for me.

00:00:11.601 --> 00:00:13.100
-Why was that embarrassing?

00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:16.167
-Well, I had just gotten off
the flight to see my dad

00:00:16.167 --> 00:00:18.334
and I came here and I,
like, looked disgusting.

00:00:18.334 --> 00:00:20.834
And I was just, kind of hiding
in the dressing room,

00:00:20.834 --> 00:00:23.133
and my dad's friend was like,
"Oh, do you want to go upstairs

00:00:23.133 --> 00:00:25.200
and, like, check out
the 'SNL' floor?"

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:26.767
And I was like, "Sure.

00:00:26.767 --> 00:00:28.901
Like, hope I don't run into
anyone, whatever."

00:00:28.901 --> 00:00:31.701
Harry Styles was hosting,
and I knew that, but I --

00:00:31.701 --> 00:00:34.400
I was like, "There's no way I'm
going to see him, right?"

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:37.100
And then, the first thing --

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:40.133
Like, I walked into the room,
and he was right there.

00:00:40.133 --> 00:00:43.000
And I literally,
like, could not --

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:44.234
Like, I went into shock.

00:00:44.234 --> 00:00:46.300
Like, I didn't even know what to
do with myself.

00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:49.033
And then I --
Yeah, I just went into a panic

00:00:49.033 --> 00:00:51.033
and then I got back down to
the dressing room

00:00:51.033 --> 00:00:54.200
and started hysterically crying

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:57.300
because I was so overwhelmed
and just not expecting that.

00:00:57.300 --> 00:01:00.367
And then you
knocked on the door.

00:01:00.367 --> 00:01:02.467
And I was so humiliated
and I hear like,

00:01:02.467 --> 00:01:03.534
"Hey, Judd, it's Jimmy."

00:01:03.534 --> 00:01:05.801
And I was like,
"Oh, no, no, no!"

00:01:05.801 --> 00:01:10.934
And then I -- Yeah, so, then I
just turned and faced the wall,

00:01:10.934 --> 00:01:13.534
like, thinking, like,
maybe if I turn around,

00:01:13.534 --> 00:01:15.501
you won't notice I was there.

00:01:15.501 --> 00:01:18.167
But the room was really small.
-Yeah.

00:01:18.167 --> 00:01:21.434
-So, yeah, and then
you saw that I was crying.

00:01:21.434 --> 00:01:24.367
And I was really humiliated by
that for like -- And I still am.

00:01:24.367 --> 00:01:26.234
Like, telling it, I'm like,
"Why am I telling this?"

00:01:26.234 --> 00:01:28.701
-Oh, no, I didn't -- That's
normally the reaction I get

00:01:28.701 --> 00:01:31.167
when I say "hi"
to people backstage.

00:01:31.167 --> 00:01:34.067
You weren't crying tonight,
I will say that.

00:01:34.067 --> 00:01:35.601
Backstage, you were not crying.

00:01:35.601 --> 00:01:37.400
But why were you nervous
for Harry?

00:01:37.400 --> 00:01:40.000
Just -- Didn't you interview him
or interview One Direction?

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:44.200
-Yeah, I did interview
One Direction when I was 14.

00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:46.767
-Now, what was this -- How did
you get a chance to do that?

00:01:46.767 --> 00:01:49.767
-I don't even --
I had a popular Twitter page

00:01:49.767 --> 00:01:50.868
when I was like 13.

00:01:50.868 --> 00:01:52.234
-Uh-huh.

00:01:52.234 --> 00:01:55.667
-And I decided I wanted
to become a child journalist,

00:01:55.667 --> 00:01:58.000
and they asked me
to interview One Direction

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:00.501
on their first trip to America.

00:02:00.501 --> 00:02:03.901
-Wow! And so that must be
nerve-racking.

00:02:03.901 --> 00:02:06.434
-Yeah, it was, like,
the scariest thing in my life.

00:02:06.434 --> 00:02:10.000
-Yeah, and I know that you were
freaking out before you --

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:11.801
right before you were
going to interview them.

00:02:11.801 --> 00:02:16.868
And you were -- You were upset,
but your dad videotaped you.

00:02:16.868 --> 00:02:18.133
-Yeah.

00:02:18.133 --> 00:02:20.167
-Well, we talked to your dad.

00:02:21.033 --> 00:02:22.334
And we have a video.

00:02:22.334 --> 00:02:24.634
If you don't mind us
showing this,

00:02:24.634 --> 00:02:26.367
this is 14-year-old Maude Apatow

00:02:26.367 --> 00:02:28.901
preparing to interview
One Direction.

00:02:28.901 --> 00:02:30.501
Here we go.
-Ooh!

00:02:30.501 --> 00:02:32.167
-In 10 minutes, you'll be in the
room with One Direction.

00:02:32.167 --> 00:02:33.467
Let's go!

00:02:40.167 --> 00:02:44.501
-What is that?
-I couldn't even say words.

00:02:44.501 --> 00:02:47.501
Like, they're just --
They weren't coming out.

00:02:47.501 --> 00:02:49.200
-We have a picture of you, too,

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:51.267
minutes before
you were interviewing them.

00:02:51.267 --> 00:02:53.300
Look at you.
You're so emotional.

00:02:53.300 --> 00:02:55.033
I mean...

00:02:55.033 --> 00:02:58.100
[ Cymbal crash ]
Oh, my gosh.

00:02:58.100 --> 00:03:00.567
Yeah, that was you.

00:03:00.567 --> 00:03:02.901
But then this is you actually
interviewing the boys,

00:03:02.901 --> 00:03:04.601
and you did a great job.

00:03:04.601 --> 00:03:07.300
-I don't know if I did such a
great job, honestly.

00:03:07.300 --> 00:03:08.901
-Oh, really? Was it bad?

00:03:08.901 --> 00:03:12.200
-I don't think--
It couldn't have been good.

00:03:12.200 --> 00:03:14.200
-Would you ever listen to it
again or play it back?

00:03:14.200 --> 00:03:15.234
-No.
-No, of course not.

00:03:15.234 --> 00:03:17.767
No, no, no.
-God no. No, no, no.

00:03:17.767 --> 00:03:19.400
-Well, shortly after that,

00:03:19.400 --> 00:03:22.868
you got to see One Direction
in concert.

00:03:22.868 --> 00:03:24.501
Your dad told us this.

00:03:24.501 --> 00:03:27.234
-I did, yes.
-And that must have been fun.

00:03:27.234 --> 00:03:30.067
It probably went -- You probably
weren't nervous then?

00:03:30.067 --> 00:03:32.367
-No. It was worse then.

00:03:32.367 --> 00:03:39.701
-So, we have a video of you
right after the concert.

00:03:39.701 --> 00:03:41.234
So, you saw the concert.
You had a great time.

00:03:41.234 --> 00:03:42.234
-Yeah.

00:03:42.234 --> 00:03:43.601
-And then,
this is after the concert

00:03:43.601 --> 00:03:45.501
with your family
and your sister.

00:03:45.501 --> 00:03:48.000
And here's -- Yeah, take a look.

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:50.000
-[ Crying ]

00:03:54.434 --> 00:03:56.868
-Maude, you're fine.

00:04:00.167 --> 00:04:02.467
-"Maude, you're fine."

00:04:02.467 --> 00:04:04.300
-Oh, my God.

00:04:05.400 --> 00:04:08.300
-You have good parents
to send that video to us,

00:04:08.300 --> 00:04:11.300
so thank you to --
We appreciate that.

00:04:11.300 --> 00:04:13.601
How is the family?
Everyone good?

00:04:13.601 --> 00:04:15.300
-Yeah, everyone's great.
-Alright. We're fans.

00:04:15.300 --> 00:04:17.200
Please say "hi"
to everyone over there.

00:04:17.200 --> 00:04:18.834
I want to talk about "Euphoria."

00:04:18.834 --> 00:04:21.167
This is a...
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:21.167 --> 00:04:26.801
...massive, massive, massive hit
on HBO this season.

00:04:26.801 --> 00:04:29.601
Bigger than anything
in the world.

00:04:29.601 --> 00:04:30.701
And everyone was
talking about it, like,

00:04:30.701 --> 00:04:33.601
broke ratings records,
all this stuff.

00:04:33.601 --> 00:04:36.667
But it's more finding
the backstories

00:04:36.667 --> 00:04:38.033
of a lot of
the characters on this one.

00:04:38.033 --> 00:04:42.400
Now, what can we expect for your
character, for Lexi?

00:04:42.400 --> 00:04:46.033
-I think you'll see a lot more
of my character this season.

00:04:46.033 --> 00:04:47.634
I don't know if
I can even say anything.

00:04:47.634 --> 00:04:48.901
I'm going to get in trouble.
-Yeah, I know.

00:04:48.901 --> 00:04:50.601
-But it's all exciting,

00:04:50.601 --> 00:04:52.968
and I think people
are going to be surprised.

00:04:52.968 --> 00:04:56.000
I think, like, people think
my character is sort of

00:04:56.000 --> 00:04:58.868
this shy, like, sweet one,
but I think she might be

00:04:58.868 --> 00:05:01.067
just as crazy as everyone else.

00:05:01.067 --> 00:05:03.367
-Oh, my gosh. No, you're --

00:05:03.367 --> 00:05:06.367
-No, she's not.
-Alright.

00:05:06.367 --> 00:05:08.000
I don't know
if I can handle that.

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:09.234
You were telling me,
though, backstage

00:05:09.234 --> 00:05:11.200
that every shot is
very technical on that show.

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:12.467
-It is very technical.

00:05:12.467 --> 00:05:14.901
So, they'll, like,
do these long shots

00:05:14.901 --> 00:05:19.467
where they don't make any edits,
so they'll have us, like,

00:05:19.467 --> 00:05:20.934
walking through
the school hallways,

00:05:20.934 --> 00:05:23.801
and it will be like
two minutes without any cuts.

00:05:23.801 --> 00:05:27.133
So if you mess up,
the whole shot is destroyed,

00:05:27.133 --> 00:05:30.367
and I always mess it up.

00:05:30.367 --> 00:05:31.667
So then, yeah, basically --

00:05:31.667 --> 00:05:34.033
-So if you mess up,
everyone has to redo the --

00:05:34.033 --> 00:05:36.067
-And it became,
like, a running joke

00:05:36.067 --> 00:05:37.968
that I would always
miss my mark.

00:05:37.968 --> 00:05:39.400
Because they put,
like, a tiny, little piece

00:05:39.400 --> 00:05:40.767
of tape on the ground.

00:05:40.767 --> 00:05:41.968
And you can't look at it,

00:05:41.968 --> 00:05:43.367
because then it's obvious
you're trying to find it.

00:05:43.367 --> 00:05:44.667
-Yeah, that is true.

00:05:44.667 --> 00:05:46.567
So you just have to,
like, zone and find the mark,

00:05:46.567 --> 00:05:48.400
and you'll be like -- So,
they'll do the tracking shot,

00:05:48.400 --> 00:05:50.267
and then you got to be like...

00:05:50.267 --> 00:05:51.300
"Hey --" You know, whatever.

00:05:51.300 --> 00:05:52.300
-Exactly!

00:05:52.300 --> 00:05:53.300
-And they're like,
"No, over here."

00:05:53.300 --> 00:05:54.400
And you go, "Oh, yeah."
"Hey!"

00:05:54.400 --> 00:05:56.133
-I'm always like
10 inches off of the mark.

00:05:56.133 --> 00:05:57.534
-Just a little bit off.

00:05:57.534 --> 00:05:59.534
-But then they were like --
They started putting, like,

00:05:59.534 --> 00:06:03.801
sandbags and boxes so I would
just, like, knock into it.

00:06:03.801 --> 00:06:06.000
-You have to walk into a wall
to hit your mark?

00:06:06.000 --> 00:06:09.167
-Yeah, it still didn't work.

00:06:09.167 --> 00:06:12.934
-Yeah, I had one line in
"Band of Brothers,"

00:06:12.934 --> 00:06:14.801
this miniseries on HBO.

00:06:14.801 --> 00:06:15.934
And Tom Hanks was directing.

00:06:15.934 --> 00:06:19.300
And I had to drive
a World War II Jeep

00:06:19.300 --> 00:06:20.567
and then say like, "Hey, boys,

00:06:20.567 --> 00:06:22.234
I'm getting the ammo"
or something.

00:06:22.234 --> 00:06:23.534
And I go, "Great, let's do it."

00:06:23.534 --> 00:06:24.968
And they go, "Oh, we got to wait
for it be nighttime."

00:06:24.968 --> 00:06:26.434
I go, "Nighttime?"

00:06:26.434 --> 00:06:28.033
And then he goes,
"We got to get the extras."

00:06:28.033 --> 00:06:29.667
And they had 200 extras.

00:06:29.667 --> 00:06:32.434
I had to drive through all
of these soldiers

00:06:32.434 --> 00:06:36.000
trying to find my mark, where
I'm driving a car to my mark

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:37.801
and then say,
"I'm bringing ammo."

00:06:37.801 --> 00:06:40.501
And I was maybe
like a mile off the mark.

00:06:40.501 --> 00:06:42.434
So I drove in
and then just parked.

00:06:42.434 --> 00:06:44.667
I go, "We got ammo, boys!
We got it."

00:06:44.667 --> 00:06:46.501
And then Tom was way over there.

00:06:46.501 --> 00:06:48.267
I was like,
"Where is everybody?"

00:06:48.267 --> 00:06:50.467
He was like, "Dude,
you're way off the mark, buddy.

00:06:50.467 --> 00:06:53.534
Can we replace him right now?
He's so bad."

00:06:53.534 --> 00:06:55.200
But you were phenomenal in this,

00:06:55.200 --> 00:06:57.467
and everyone is buzzing
and talking about you.

00:06:57.467 --> 00:06:59.801
Congratulations
on all the success.

00:06:59.801 --> 00:07:02.334
-Thank you!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:02.334 --> 00:07:04.167
-I want to show everyone a clip.

00:07:04.167 --> 00:07:06.501
Here's Maude Apatow
in "Euphoria."

00:07:06.501 --> 00:07:07.801
Take a look.

00:07:07.801 --> 00:07:09.234
-How you doing?

00:07:09.234 --> 00:07:11.868
-I'm good. Um...

00:07:11.868 --> 00:07:12.934
-Hi.

00:07:12.934 --> 00:07:14.567
I'm Faye.

00:07:14.567 --> 00:07:17.133
-I'm Lexi. Um...

00:07:18.234 --> 00:07:20.367
Are -- are you guys --

00:07:20.367 --> 00:07:24.167
-Yeah, no, she's just staying
with me for a bit,

00:07:24.167 --> 00:07:26.534
but -- but she's cool though.

00:07:27.667 --> 00:07:29.901
What brings you out here anyway?

00:07:32.200 --> 00:07:34.734
-Oh, I just came to get
a-a drink.

00:07:37.367 --> 00:07:41.534
-Okay, well,
we got plenty of those.

00:07:41.534 --> 00:07:45.467
Uh, do you need help
finding anything?

00:07:45.467 --> 00:07:47.934
-No, I'm okay.

00:07:47.934 --> 00:07:51.901
-Oh, uh, that's the malt liquor.

00:07:53.501 --> 00:07:55.434
-Yeah, I know.

00:07:55.434 --> 00:07:57.934
-What?!

00:08:01.267 --> 00:08:02.801
Maude Apatow, everybody!

00:08:02.801 --> 00:08:07.133
"Euphoria" airs Sundays at
9:00 p.m. on HBO and HBO Max.

